{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1187498-creating-dross","id":1187498,"title":"Creating Dross","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-19T02:22:55-08:00","id":1187498,"title":"Creating Dross","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> Please help me out:<br /> <br /> How can a changeling create Dross?<br /> I know a sure way: Kill a Chimera and process it. It's not so appealing.<br /> <br /> Is it possible to use your own Glamour as a source or siphon Balefire to create it?<br /> <br /> Thank you,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T06:04:58-08:00","id":1187527,"title":"","content":"Lots of great art created is dross as well. So you can get Glamour from destroying great works of art instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T17:43:40-08:00","id":1187701,"title":"","content":"You can collect Dross from natural locations where the Dreaming touches the Autumn World if I remember right, though there is no doubt a Chimera or two might be protecting these places. Destroying works of art like expressed above I believe might cause a banality trigger? Not quite sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T18:29:01-08:00","id":1187709,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, on looking through C20 again it looks like they may have taken out works of art as dross?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T19:17:06-08:00","id":1187720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1187498-creating-dross?p=1187709#post1187709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, on looking through C20 again it looks like they may have taken out works of art as dross?</div> </div> </div> </div>If so I still treat them as Dross as well as the written word since strong emotions are poured into them. The destruction of such an item though while yielding glamour can also damage the dreams and emotions tied to the item such as tearing up a lovers note in front of the writer, burning the manuscript for someone's life work, or in one case I remember the destruction of a original manuscript of Shakespeare. Doing so is harmful for everyone involved as it destroys the threads of myths, emotions, and dreams that made such an item resonate strongly with glamour from the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> One of my players is running around for example with a first edition copy of the Princess of Mars that's is heavily read but is infused with glamour from the countless readers who read and dreamt of their own adventures and the legacy ERB left in his works. It is a potent piece of Dross because of all the threads we have tied to it as a tale of science fantasy and romance with another world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T04:50:26-08:00","id":1187805,"title":"","content":"I *think* that destroying precious artwork is a Banal action with more drawbacks than merits.<br /> <br /> They could inspire dozens-&gt;thousands of humans, creating Dreams. I would do such as last resort.<br /> <br /> In the past they were handful types of dross (for example dreamstones), but I don't really know, where do they come from. Destroying Chimeras, something living, breathing &amp; beautiful (I find my nightmares most beautiful, beacuse they stir the most emotion.) to get some temporaly boost is not a clever bargain","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T05:06:27-08:00","id":1187808,"title":"","content":"I don't think having a Seelie bias to that degree in the system is a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T05:16:46-08:00","id":1187810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1187498-creating-dross?p=1187808#post1187808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think having a Seelie bias to that degree in the system is a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm in my current character mindset.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I still find the information of Dross seriously lacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T02:19:30-08:00","id":1189811,"title":"","content":"C20 p264 under Rhapsody has rules about destroying works of art and the Banality Triggers on p269 include 'willfully destroying an irreplaceable faerie artifact' which a cunning storyteller could expand to include such works of art.<br /> <br /> Also, calling that 'Seelie Bias' is way over doing it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T04:46:54-08:00","id":1189828,"title":"","content":"I meant it promotes the Seelie as being objectively right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T22:14:12-08:00","id":1190570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1187498-creating-dross?p=1189828#post1189828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant it promotes the Seelie as being objectively right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nay, the Unseelie Code states that the Glamour is &quot;an eternally replenishable resource&quot;, and not that is an aternally replenishing one.<br /> Yes, there are sociopaths like Forsworne Prince who throw Glamour like free candies, but others should understand that stuff in a finite system should be finite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T09:54:37-08:00","id":1190697,"title":"","content":"It is curious that the C20 rulebook mentions that dross is often exchanged amongst changelings but that the same rulebook gives only the example of harvesting it from dead chimera.<br /> <br /> Are we meant to draw the conclusion that Changelings are regularly trotting off on hunts in the dreaming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T09:59:50-08:00","id":1191024,"title":"","content":"What about drawing Glamour and dross from online sources ? I can think of a great deal of ravaging that takes place online.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T14:31:15-08:00","id":1191453,"title":"","content":"IIRC, any kind of epiphany usually needs to be done face to face. The changeling needs to be able to establish a phychic connection. I could see a treasure computer (or if you want to really get wild, a treasure web browser) that allows that kind of connection to be made over the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T04:24:35-07:00","id":1194204,"title":"","content":"Dross is kinda a big thing in many games, because changelings can only store small quantities of Glamour themselves. You might want to be quite flexible in how you use it.<br /> <br /> I made a house rule about locations creating dross if they've been used for a long time for creative purposes. For every uninterrupted year of such use, I rule that the ambient Glamour manifests as one point of dross per month, to a maximum of one point per week. Longer than that, and it gets real consideration for becoming a freehold, glade, etc. This dross might manifest as magic fungus, strange crystals or colourful moulds in the chimerical world.<br /> <br /> I prefer the idea of an important artwork releasing Glamour over time, rather than only upon destruction (which sounds like a Banality trigger to me, if it was a unique or rare item). Similarly, we also allow frequent rolls for Glamour throughout the creative process, since there are usually multiple epiphanies (and focusing entirely on 'product' feels Banal). <br /> <br /> We determine that the first roll to figure out how long it takes to get to know the dreamer also indicates the time period after which the changeling can re-roll for epiphany. So if you roll high (meaning you build rapport quicker), you also get to roll more often. Incomplete artworks can even reap some minor rewards--it's the process, not the result, that's important. Getting dreamers to make longer works thus has its advantages.<br /> <br /> Conversely, destroying mass-manufactured art as part of a bunk could be a creative endeavour if it's making a radical statement about throwaway consumerism or whatever. Destroying postcard prints of 'The Kiss' is materially different to destroying the original canvas, after all.<br /> <br /> You could also use Arts creatively to imbue Glamour into an item, thus creating dross. Or, if you want characters to be able to store more Glamour than their permanent trait (which reduces the need for dross), you could use something similar to the cramming rules for ghouls. So you take in more Glamour than your permanent trait, say, but you take Nightmare Dice for every point over, which makes it more dangerous to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}